{#
  AICE Design Language — Side Navigation Layout

  Use for: content pages with a persistent left-rail navigation listing
  the sections of a manual or reference guide (broader than section.njk's
  in-section nav). Renders a one-quarter sidebar using the navigation partial
  and a three-quarters content area.

  Expected template variables:
    title      — page heading (h1) and browser tab prefix
    content    — Markdown string for the main body
    supportBox — { title?, description?, items? } — enables the support box (optional)

  The navigation partial (partials/navigation.njk) renders a static list of
  manual sections using govuk-list. Customise that partial for your project.
#}
{% extends "layouts/page.njk" %}

{% block content %}
<div class="govuk-grid-row">

  {# Sidebar — manual section navigation ───────────────────────────────────
    Uses govuk-list with govuk-link items. aria-current is applied via
    the `currentUrl` template variable compared against each item's href.
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-one-quarter">
    {% include "partials/navigation.njk" %}
  </div>

  <div class="govuk-grid-column-three-quarters">
    <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">{{ title }}</h1>
    {{ content | markdown | safe }}
    {% include "partials/support-box.njk" %}
  </div>

</div>
{% endblock %}
